#. type: Title =
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "OpenEMS: § 14a EnWG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"§ 14a of the German Energy Industry Act (EnWG) regulates “controllable "
"consumption devices” in Germany: heat pumps, wallboxes, air conditioning "
"units and also electricity storage systems that can charge from the grid. "
"The grid operator may temporarily limit their grid purchase if there is a "
"risk of overload. In return, there are reduced grid fees; with “Module 3” "
"they are time-variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid "OpenEMS has two building blocks for this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"the **power limitation of the storage** in response to a signal from the "
"grid operator,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**time-variable grid fees (Module 3)** as part of the electricity prices for "
"xref:user/storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[time-of-use tariffs]."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 1: Power limitation of the storage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-the-function
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The limitation is handled by the controller **Controller.Ess.Limiter14a** "
"(usually `+ctrlEssLimiter14a0+`). It has only two settings:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Setting\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| Ess-ID\n"
"| the storage that is limited (usually `+ess0+`)\n"
"| Input Channel\n"
"| the input at which the signal from the grid operator is present, e.g. a contact of a control box\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What happens on a signal"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"If the signal from the grid operator is present, **OpenEMS limits the "
"charging power of the storage to a maximum of 4.2 kW**. More precisely:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The storage power may not fall below −4,200 W. Charging is therefore "
"possible with a maximum of 4.2 kW."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid "**Discharging remains possible without limitation.**"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The limitation applies **to any charging**, even if the power comes from "
"your own PV system. OpenEMS does not distinguish here where the charging "
"energy comes from."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"It only takes effect in **grid mode**. In island mode (emergency power) "
"there is no limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-happens-on-a-signal
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The limitation has **priority** over all other storage functions: the § 14a "
"controller runs first in the defined order, even before the ripple control "
"receiver, emergency reserve, price control, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Signal logic"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-signal-logic
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The input is evaluated **inverted** (noted in the code as a peculiarity of "
"the relay board): the limitation is active when the input reports “off”. If "
"the input does not supply any value at all, e.g. in the event of a fault, "
"there is **no** limitation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Value\n"
"| Meaning\n"
"\n"
"| `+RestrictionMode+`\n"
"| whether the limitation is currently active\n"
"| `+CumulatedRestrictionTime+`\n"
"| total duration of limitation (seconds)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"Both values are stored with high priority in the xref:user/data/history-"
"rrd4j.adoc[history]. This makes it possible to prove later when and for how "
"long the grid operator intervened."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-display-in-the-web-interface
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"If the § 14a function is set up, an additional line appears in the **grid "
"widget**. During a limitation it shows the value “4.2 kW”."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-display-in-the-web-interface
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"In the **grid history**, periods with active limitation are marked in the "
"chart, similar to ripple control receiver interventions and island mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**As an app:** “App.Ess.Limiter14a” in the app center. You select the "
"storage and an input contact. There can only be one such app."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**For FENECON Home and Commercial systems:** The system app has the option "
"“Has limiter for §14a”. If it is set, the limitation is set up "
"automatically; the first digital input of the control computer is used as "
"the input (`+…/DigitalInput1+`). The option can only be selected if the "
"control computer has its own switching inputs and outputs (CM3, CM4, CM4S, "
"CM4S Gen2 or Gen3); otherwise it is grayed out."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "What does not exist (yet)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-not-exist-yet
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**Heat pump and wallbox:** The code has no separate § 14a limitation for "
"heat pumps or charge points. The function only affects the storage. For "
"other devices, the limitation takes place, if at all, outside OpenEMS, e.g. "
"directly via the control input of the device."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-not-exist-yet
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**Energy optimizer:** The limit value of 4.2 kW is stored in the optimizer, "
"but is not used anywhere in the current code. The xref:user/schedule/"
"overview.adoc[schedule] therefore does not take a § 14a limitation into "
"account. This would hardly be possible anyway, because an intervention by "
"the grid operator cannot be foreseen."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-not-exist-yet
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**Ongoing operation with price control:** The limitation is nevertheless "
"complied with during operation. The § 14a controller runs before xref:user/"
"storage-control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[price control]. Its setpoint is "
"therefore limited to a maximum of 4.2 kW charging power."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-not-exist-yet
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**Consequence for the schedule:** If “Charge from grid” is planned for the "
"time of an intervention, less is charged than intended. The storage then "
"also cannot absorb PV surplus above 4.2 kW; it goes into the grid or is "
"curtailed if there is a feed-in limit. At the next planning, the optimizer "
"continues calculating with the actual state of charge."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-what-does-not-exist-yet
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"**Fixed value:** The 4.2 kW are permanently stored in the code and cannot be "
"adjusted."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part 2: Time-variable grid fees (Module 3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-part-2-time-variable-grid-fees-module-3
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid "With Module 3, different grid fees apply depending on the time of day:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Level\n"
"| Abbreviation\n"
"| typical\n"
"\n"
"| Low tariff\n"
"| NT\n"
"| at night, e.g. 0–5\n"
"| Standard tariff\n"
"| ST\n"
"| remaining time\n"
"| High tariff\n"
"| HT\n"
"| in the evening, e.g. 17–21\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"In the tariff app (e.g. for ENTSO-E exchange prices), for the bidding zone "
"Germany there is the question **“Do you use time-variable network charges "
"according to Section 14a EnWG (Module 3)?”**. If you answer yes, you select "
"the grid operator:"
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"For some large grid operators, the grid fees are **permanently stored** in "
"the code: Bayernwerk, Netze BW, EWE Netz, MITNETZ, SH Netz, Westnetz, E.DIS, "
"Avacon, LEW, “TE Netze” (in the code `+TE_NETZE+`) and Netze ODR. The prices "
"in ct/kWh and the time windows are stored, per quarter in each case."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"For “Other”, you enter the time windows for NT and HT yourself; ST applies "
"to times without an entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-setup-2
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The grid fees are then added to the exchange price as additional costs. This "
"way, they are included in the electricity price that xref:user/storage-"
"control/time-of-use-tariffs.adoc[price control] uses for planning. This "
"makes grid charging more attractive in NT times, for example, and less "
"attractive in HT times."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The stored grid fees only apply to the **quarters entered in the code**. If "
"a grid operator changes its prices or a new year is added, OpenEMS must be "
"updated. The price cannot be determined for times without an entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"The grid fees in the code should be compared with the current price sheet of "
"your own grid operator. If there are differences, “Other” with your own time "
"windows is the safer choice."
msgstr ""

#. type: #sec-good-to-know
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
msgid ""
"Module 3 only affects the **price calculation**. It has nothing to do "
"technically with the power limitation from Part 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: modules/ROOT/pages/user/storage-control/section-14a-enwg.adoc
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| \n"
"| Power limitation\n"
"| Time-variable grid fees (Module 3)\n"
"\n"
"| Purpose\n"
"| Reducing grid purchase on the instructions of the grid operator\n"
"| Using lower grid fees at certain times\n"
"| affects\n"
"| only the storage (charging at a maximum of 4.2 kW)\n"
"| the electricity price for price control\n"
"| triggered by\n"
"| Signal at the input (e.g. control box)\n"
"| Time of day (fixed time windows)\n"
"| Setup\n"
"| App “Limiter14a” or option in the Home/Commercial app\n"
"| Option in the tariff app, selection of the grid operator\n"
msgstr ""
